# [DD-13b.W23.3] §2.27's WHOLE PROMISE IN ONE CELL, and it is an
# ACCEPTANCE fixture on purpose.
#
# `ext <consumer>` is the AUX production: consumer-namespaced, parsed
# STRUCTURALLY so a malformed aux block cannot corrupt what follows, and
# semantically UNINTERPRETED — dumped faithfully and read by no build, no
# check and no config resolution. Its failure mode is therefore pcrec
# deciding it UNDERSTANDS something, and that is a failure an acceptance
# fixture catches and a refusal fixture structurally cannot: every key
# below is a word pcrec has never heard of, and all three legs must take
# them without asking what any of them means.
#
# The consumer name is a free `defname` resolved against nothing at all.
# S-R6 (S245) is the plant this is the first detector for: flipping the
# `ext` rows' `children` from `tree` to a named scope makes leg A refuse
# what it must accept, which is aux being NARROWED.
#
# LEG A ONLY, AND THE REASON IS THE SEAM RULING RATHER THAN THIS LANE'S
# SCOPE. `ext` at FILE scope is a HEAD declaration, the head has exactly
# one parser (w1_impl §1.1), and legs B and C never read those bytes —
# leg B takes the body's start line off `--list-source` and leg C refuses
# a head-bearing file by name. So a three-leg assertion on a file-scope
# `ext` is not available at any point in W23, exactly as r59-A2 found for
# `dup_head_description.rxtin`. The BLOCK-scope half of the same
# production is asserted on all three legs by `aux_deep_tree.rxtin`,
# `aux_literal_pipe.rxtin`, `aux_malformed_body.rxtin` and
# `aux_subtree_extent.rxtin`, every one of which is headless on purpose.
ext bench
  roster pcre2 re2 hyperscan
  matrix
    rows 16
    columns 4
    seed 20260915
  policy strict
  weighting inverse-frequency

pattern a+
ext bench
  weight 3
  regime throughput
m "aaa" 0 3
